The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/architecture/arch-04-port-slot-accumulation.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

- **6 findings total**: 0 High, 3 Medium, 3 Low
- **Key issues**:
  - The declarative wiring model is weakened because `from_declarations()` unconditionally creates thermal accumulators for every env zone, so misconfigured equipment targeting a wrong (but valid) zone won't error
  - `apply_occupancy_gains()` bypasses the `accumulate()` API and silently drops gains if no accumulator matches
  - `refresh_equipment_caches()` doesn't rebuild `PortSlots`, so dynamically added equipment may crash on undeclared targets
  - HPWH compressor waste heat is conflated with `JacketLoss` (diagnostic-only impact)
- **Verified correct**:
  - `PortSlots::accumulate()` properly rejects truly undeclared zones/loops/domains (tested)
  - All 19 equipment types have correct `ThermalCategory` tags
  - Multi-equipment accumulation to same zone works correctly
  - Zone ID indexing uses opaque `u16` with equality comparison, not slice indexing — no off-by-one risk
